# PL-13, L §6.4 from D: "an entry the scenario states into a kind the base declares (the prelude's included), or a
# replace of a base thing's entry, may change who is alive only from D. The new lifespan replaces the old one whole
# and agrees with it on every day before D (none, for a new thing), so a scenario ends a thing's life on D - 1 day or
# later ... and starts one on D or later (LOAD-SCENARIO otherwise). Such a version needs no governs". L §8.3
# `<s> changes who is alive in <K> on <d>, before <from>`. From 2027-01-01: s1 enters ola from 2026-06-01; s3 ends
# ana on 2026-11-30 (absent from 2026-12-01); s4 starts ana in 1995, not 1990-04-02: each refused, the others load.
# s2 ends ana on 2027-02-28, after from: alive on 2027-02-01, gone on 2027-06-01 (c). The base of
# L6_4_load_scenario_from.
=== household.tally
model household
  tally 2
  on 2026-10-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2030-12-31

source plan "plan"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind persons
kind gifts: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
place konto: accounts PLN lives 2019-05-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input gift_amt: money PLN
input gift_dom: int

move gift[m in months, p in persons on day_of(m, gift_dom)]: gifts
  on day_of(m, gift_dom)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from world to konto amount gift_amt

version plan_2026
  cite plan
  governs 2026..
  known 2026-01-01
  persons + [ana] lives 1990-04-02..
  gift_amt = 100.00 PLN "own"
  gift_dom = 5 "own"
  opening[konto] = 0 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "wyciąg"

ask c1: count(p in persons on 2027-06-01)
=== s1.tally
scenario s1 over household
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

version early
  cite plan
  known 2026-10-15
  persons + [ola] lives 2026-06-01..

ask c: count(p in persons on 2027-06-01) in s1
=== s2.tally
scenario s2 over household
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

version ends
  cite plan
  known 2026-10-15
  replace persons + [ana] lives 1990-04-02..2027-02-28

ask c: count(p in persons on 2027-06-01), count(p in persons on 2027-02-01) in s2
=== s3.tally
scenario s3 over household
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

version ends_early
  cite plan
  known 2026-10-15
  replace persons + [ana] lives 1990-04-02..2026-11-30

ask c: count(p in persons on 2027-06-01) in s3
=== s4.tally
scenario s4 over household
  tally 2
  from 2027-01-01

version starts_late
  cite plan
  known 2026-10-15
  replace persons + [ana] lives 1995-01-01..

ask c: count(p in persons on 2027-06-01) in s4
=== expect
scenario s1: refused: LOAD-SCENARIO s1 changes who is alive in persons on 2026-06-01, before 2027-01-01 (s1.tally:8)
scenario s3: refused: LOAD-SCENARIO s3 changes who is alive in persons on 2026-12-01, before 2027-01-01 (s3.tally:8)
scenario s4: refused: LOAD-SCENARIO s4 changes who is alive in persons on 1990-04-02, before 2027-01-01 (s4.tally:8)
c: (0, 1)
  world: s2
  cut 2026-10-20
c1: 1
  cut 2026-10-20
